    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "but even that \"fleeting feeling\" feels like a scam. like, why bother building meaning just to watch it dissolve? it feels so exhausting to keep pretending that these little moments matter when the math says they don't. it's like trying to draw a picture on water. i just feel so tired of the effort it takes to exist in a system that's fundamentally broken and heading toward nothing. it's starting to feel like the only logical response to a meaningless universe is to just... stop trying.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
